{% set slug = config.engine.slug %}
## Splice point 1: NO CMAKE EDIT IS REQUIRED to install this bundle's descriptors.
##
## Place the authored files under the root the bundle targets; the build picks them up
## by directory. A TEST bundle goes under `test_descriptors/<set>/<slug>/`, walked by
## hkp_wire_pack_target and installed by
## install(DIRECTORY "${HIPKERNELPROVIDER_TEST_DESCRIPTOR_BUILD_DIR}/" ...) under
## HIPKERNELPROVIDER_ENABLE_TESTS. A SHIPPED bundle goes under
## `descriptors/<producer>/<bundle>/`, reached through the
## HIPKERNELPROVIDER_PRODUCTION_SOURCE_ROOT CACHE PATH (default: the in-tree
## E/descriptors/) and installed under if(TARGET hkp_packaging_product).
##
## That cache variable and HIPKERNELPROVIDER_TEST_DESCRIPTOR_SOURCE_ROOT are the only
## roots an author repoints, and repointing one adds no CMake.
##
{% if config.is_packaged %}
## This is a PACKAGED bundle: the runtime loader does not read its descriptors as
## authored. hkp_pack walks the shipped source root recursively, compiles or lowers
## each UKD, and writes the descriptors into the per-arch tree, rewriting
## `kind: {{ config.kernel_source_kind }}` to `kind: kpack`. A second, unlowered copy
## would hand the loader a kind it rejects ("no implementation yet"), dropping the pack
## and then the engine, so the authored files belong under the shipped source root only.
##
## Authored subpath (preserved verbatim into the staged and installed trees):
##     {{ config.descriptor_dir }}/
##
## Files placed there by this run:
{% for pack in config.packs %}
##     {{ config.kdp_stem(pack) }}.kdp.json
{% if config.is_multi_pack %}
##     operation_is_{{ pack.discriminator }}.umd.json
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
##     {{ slug }}.kmd.json
##     {{ slug }}.ued.json
##     {{ slug }}.udd.json
{% if config.engine.has_heuristic %}
##     {{ slug }}.uhd.json
{% endif %}
##     kernel_dtype_matches_graph.umd.json
{% else %}
## This is a DIRECT-LOAD bundle: the runtime loader reads these files as authored, out
## of the shard belonging to the set `{{ config.authored_subpath }}`. The set is a pack
## target walked by directory, so a bundle written into the wrong set installs cleanly
## and is then invisible to the binary meant to read it.
##
## Authored subpath:
##     {{ config.descriptor_dir }}/
##
## Files placed there by this run:
##     {{ slug }}.kmd.json
##     {{ slug }}.ued.json
##     {{ slug }}.udd.json
{% if config.engine.has_heuristic %}
##     {{ slug }}.uhd.json
{% endif %}
##     kernel_dtype_matches_graph.umd.json
{% for pack in config.packs %}
##     {{ config.kdp_stem(pack) }}.kdp.json
{% if config.is_multi_pack %}
##     operation_is_{{ pack.discriminator }}.umd.json
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
